4422..4497 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every loop: the round trip at a variable, by"
4498..4576 Comment "/// induction over the words. The result type reads the word the fold descends"
4577..4651 Comment "/// on, so each arm answers it at its letter and the recursive call at the"
4652..4724 Comment "/// rest: `sect[<](q)` relates `spin(wind(q))` to `q`, and carried along"
4725..4805 Comment "/// `loopOn` it relates `loop ∷ spin(wind(q))`, which `spin(wind(loop ∷ q))`"
4806..4885 Comment "/// runs to, to `loop ∷ q`. The case respects the cancellations: at `loop ∷"
4886..4962 Comment "/// back(loop) ∷ q` the arms compose to `cong(loopOn, cong(unloopOn, p))`,"
4963..5037 Comment "/// whose functions compose to the identity under the words\' rules, so the"
5038..5081 Comment "/// chain is `p` itself, the answer at `q`."
